  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is RNA-only multiprofile with avgpool, where scvi_n200 outperforms pca_n200 (0.650 vs 0.591 accuracy) and avgpool outperforms transformer for pca. The main remaining uncertainty among unimodal RNA designs is whether scgpt can match or exceed scvi under the same profile and aggregation setting. config_008 tests this cleanly by changing only the RNA encoder while keeping multiprofile and avgpool fixed. This is a good use of the next experiment because it identifies the best RNA representation before spending budget on more complex multimodal or fusion variants."
}

